  "issue_title": "feat(adapters): add a DROP reading-comprehension adapter (discrete reasoning, EM/token-F1 scoring, no code execution)",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\nAdd **DROP** (Discrete Reasoning Over Paragraphs) \u2014 the reading-comprehension benchmark that requires discrete reasoning over a passage (arithmetic, counting, sorting, span selection) \u2014 as a first-class benchmark: a `drop.py` adapter that loads the passage/question items and grades answers with DROP's official **exact-match + token-F1** metric (number/date/span normalization). Pure text scoring \u2014 **no code execution, no\nsandbox**. Default config and every existing benchmark are unchanged.\n\n## Goal / Motivation\n\nThe router's benchmark coverage is math (MATH-500/AIME), MCQ knowledge/reasoning (MMLU/MMLU-Pro/GPQA/BBH), and code (LiveCodeBench/SWE-bench). **DROP has no adapter or loader**, so a standard *reading-comprehension-with-reasoning* benchmark can't be trained or evaluated on. DROP is distinctive: answers are numbers, dates, or **sets of text spans** grounded in a passage, graded by a normalized token-F1 (not a single letter or exact string), so it exercises a different routing regime \u2014 extract-and-reason over long context \u2014 than anything currently in the suite. Like the MCQ adapters (and unlike the code\nadapters) it is graded by comparing text, so it needs **no runner and no isolation**.\n\n## Proposal\n\nA self-contained adapter, fully offline-testable (guarded HF loader with a toy fallback;\nscoring is pure string/number math).\n\n1. **`src/trinity/adapters/drop.py`** \u2014 `task_type` free-form (`MATH`-family, since answers\n   are short strings/numbers):\n   - `DropReference` \u2014 structured reference: the set of acceptable gold answers\n     (`answers`, each rendered to a string from DROP's number/date/spans validated answer),\n     with `to_dict`/`from_dict`/`is_valid`.\n   - `load_drop_tasks(split, max_items, seed)` \u2014 lazy/guarded HuggingFace loader\n     (`ucinlp/drop`) with an offline toy fallback; normalized `Task`s carrying the passage\n     + question in the prompt and the gold answer set in the reference.\n   - `build_drop_prompt(passage, question)` \u2014 the passage/question format with an explicit\n     \"give only the concise answer\" instruction.\n   - **DROP metric** (the substance): `_normalize` (lowercase, strip articles/punctuation,\n     collapse whitespace, number normalization), `_em` (exact match), and `_token_f1`\n     (bag-of-tokens F1 over the answer set, DROP's official multi-span rule). `score_drop`\n     extracts the candidate's final answer and returns the binary reward `1.0` iff the\n     token-F1 against the best-matching gold answer is `1.0` (equivalently EM for single\n     answers; correct multiset for multi-span answers).\n   - `DropAdapter` \u2014 `load_tasks` / `build_prompt` / `score_output` (no runner; DROP never\n     executes code), overriding `score_trajectory` to grade the final answer.\n2. **Registry** \u2014 register `drop` on import; update the registry-isolation test's restore\n   list.\n3. **Tests** \u2014 `tests/test_drop_adapter.py`: schema round-trip; guarded loader + toy\n   fallback (all loader calls fake `datasets`, so no network); prompt shape; and the DROP\n   metric \u2014 number answers (`\"16\"` vs `\"16.0\"`/`\"sixteen\"`-style normalization), date and\n   span answers, multi-span bag-F1, article/punctuation/case normalization, and a\n   partial-overlap answer scoring `0.0` under the binary (F1==1) rule. Torch-free, offline.\n\nExpected size \u2248 450\u2013550 lines across adapter + tests, in line with the merged SWE-bench (#42) and BBH adapters.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] `get_adapter(\"drop\").load_tasks(...)` returns normalized `Task`s; `available_adapters()`\n      includes it.\n- [ ] `from_dict(to_dict(x)) == x`; a reference with no gold answers is `is_valid() == False`.\n- [ ] The DROP metric matches the reference behavior on canonical cases: EM after\n      normalization, token-F1 over multi-span answer sets, and article/number/date folding.\n- [ ] A correct answer scores `1.0`, a wrong or partial-overlap answer `0.0`.\n- [ ] Offline: no network, no GPU, no torch import from the adapter or its tests; **no\n      subprocess / code execution anywhere**. All loader tests fake `datasets` so CI is\n      network-independent.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/`, `ruff check src/`, `mypy src/` stay green.\n\n## Impact\n\nAdds a standard reading-comprehension-with-discrete-reasoning benchmark, broadening the routing suite into long-context extract-and-reason \u2014 with a faithful implementation of DROP's EM/token-F1 metric, **zero execution surface** (no sandbox to review), and no change to existing benchmarks or the frozen protocol.\n",
